## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a privacy-aware OTCA telemetry path at scale with per-tenant residency and multi-region replication.

## Key Concepts
- OTLP, OpenTelemetry Collector
- Kafka/Pulsar topology
- Tenant isolation & PII redaction
- Region-local immutable storage & cross-region replication
- SLA-driven sampling & drift testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-processor to redact PII in OTEL attributes
class RedactProcessor {
  process(span) {
    const redacted = ['cardNumber','email','ip'];
    redacted.forEach(k => {
      if (span.attributes[k]) span.attributes[k] = 'REDACTED';
    });
    return span;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate privacy compliance across regions?
- How would you monitor cross-region replication lag and SLA breaches?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design OTCA-compliant governance for feature flags and telemetry with strict residency, immutable records, and secure audit trails.

## Key Concepts

- OTCA residency enforcement
- Write-once ledger (Iceberg/Parquet)
- Region-scoped streaming (Kafka topics)
- Privacy masking for telemetry
- Rollback and rollout testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: region-local validation and masking
function processEvent(event){
  // enforce residency
  if (!inRegion(event.region)) throw new Error("region mismatch");
  // apply masking for sensitive fields
  event.user_id = hash(event.user_id);
  return event;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test cross-region policy drift?
- How would you enforce secret binding updates across regions?

